{"name":"Colour Blind","hex":"#c6d2de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"colour blind","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["British spelling of color blind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colour_blind"}],"entries":[{"title":"Colour Blind (Seaway album)","blocks":[{"text":"Colour Blind is the second studio album by Canadian rock band Seaway and follow-up to 2013's Hoser."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Seaway_Colour_Blind.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colour_Blind_(Seaway_album)","wikidata":"Q22075073"},{"title":"Colour Blind (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Colour Blind is a stage play by Indian playwright Manav Kaul and Kalki Koechlin. It was screened at the Sir Mutha Venkata Subba Rao Hall in Chennai, in August 2014. It starred Koechlin, Satyajit Sharma in dual roles. The play is based on the life of Indian poet Rabindranath Tagore. In an interview Kaul stated that the play is \"an attempt to see beyond the majestic Gurudev and discover the man through his relationships.\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colour_Blind_(play)","wikidata":"Q25206535"},{"title":"Color blindness","blocks":[{"text":"Color blindness or color vision deficiency (CVD) is the decreased ability to see color, differences in color, or distinguish shades of color. The severity of color blindness ranges from mostly unnoticeable to full absence of color perception."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Ishihara_9.svg/330px-Ishihara_9.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_blindness","wikidata":"Q133696"},{"title":"Color","blocks":[{"text":"Color is the visual perception produced by the activation of the different types of cone cells in the eye caused by light. Though color is not an inherent property of matter, color perception is related to an object's light absorption, emission, reflection and transmission. For most humans, visible wavelengths of light are the ones perceived in the visible light spectrum, with three types of cone cells (trichromacy). Other animals may have a different number of cone cell types or have eyes sensitive to different wavelengths, such as bees that can distinguish ultraviolet, and thus have a different color sensitivity range. Animal perception of color originates from different light wavelength or spectral sensitivity in cone cell types, which is then processed by the brain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Colouring_pencils.jpg/330px-Colouring_pencils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color","wikidata":"Q1075"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/ConeMosaics.jpg/500px-ConeMosaics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/ConeMosaics.jpg/500px-ConeMosaics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of the distribution of cone cells in the fovea of a normal trichromatic retina (left), and a protanopic retina. The center of the fovea holds very few blue-sensitive cones.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConeMosaics.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/%D0%92%D0%B5%D1%87%D1%96%D1%80_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%22%D1%96%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%96%22_-_%D1%80%D1%96%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%9F%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%91%D1%83%D0%B3.jpg/250px-%D0%92%D0%B5%D1%87%D1%96%D1%80_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%22%D1%96%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%96%22_-_%D1%80%D1%96%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%9F%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%91%D1%83%D0%B3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip